 ## 2026-07-21
 
+### 0442 — Apple VPN terminal observation registers before authoritative status (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
+- REGRESSION: Both NetworkExtension adapters read `NEVPNConnection.status` before installing `NEVPNStatusDidChange`, so a terminal transition in that gap could be lost and an already-stopped session could falsely reach the 15-second `stopTimedOut` path.
+- FIX: iOS and macOS now install the observer first and then perform an authoritative status read through an injectable seam. The locked retirement handshake also handles a synchronous terminal notification before registration returns its token: completion wins once, and the late-arriving token is immediately unregistered.
+- COVERAGE: A deterministic two-platform matrix covers terminal-before-registration, terminal-during-registration without a notification, notification-before-token-return, notification-first completion, duplicate/late notification retirement, and cancellation. Every terminal/cancel path unregisters once and produces at most one completion.
+- VERIFICATION: Focused normal and Thread Sanitizer runs each pass 33 tests; `make validate-core` passes 251 tests in 24 suites plus build; strict Swift format, tracked/untracked diff, and board validation are clean; generic iOS Simulator and macOS adapter builds succeed with signing disabled.
+
+### 0421 — VPN preference operations are non-reentrant and NSNumber versions are exact (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
+- REGRESSION: Actor isolation did not serialize repository calls across suspended NetworkExtension callbacks, so concurrent operations could load and mutate overlapping manager generations. Both platform seams also used `NSNumber.intValue`, truncating `1.5` to current version 1 and overflowing `UInt64.max` into repairable corruption.
+- FIX: Every public ensure/enable/disable/remove/repair entry point now crosses one FIFO operation gate, held through its terminal result; internal repair convergence reuses the held operation without re-entering the gate. Manager-contract inspection carries signed `Int` or unsigned `UInt64` versions without narrowing, while Boolean, fractional, and other type-confused versions fail closed with zero mutations.
+- COVERAGE: Deterministic held-callback tests queue every repository operation and prove no second load or mutation before the first terminal result; concurrent zero-manager ensure creates and saves exactly one canonical manager. Both iOS and macOS seams cover `NSNumber(true)`, `1.5`, `UInt64.max`, `Int.max`, and `Int(1)`, including zero-write ensure/enable/disable/remove/repair paths.
+- VERIFICATION: The focused suite and Thread Sanitizer each pass 27 tests. `make validate-core` passes 245 tests in 24 suites plus the post-test build; strict Swift format lint, diff/board checks, and generic iOS Simulator/macOS adapter builds pass. A first parallel platform-build attempt hit SwiftPM's shared build-database lock; the independent sequential macOS rerun succeeded.
+
+### 0405 — VPN manager rework preserves all future versions and fresh authority (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
+- REGRESSION: Future manager-contract versions were narrowed through `UInt16(exactly:)`, so 65,536 and `Int.max` fell into repairable corruption. Explicit enable also returned early when already enabled and could save during connecting, reasserting, or disconnecting.
+- FIX: Manager-contract `updateRequired` now carries the original `Int` without narrowing; every version greater than v1 remains unsupported future data. Explicit enable returns `sessionTransitionInProgress` before setters or saves for all three transitions, while an already-enabled manager still performs the user-intent setter/save/fresh-reload verification path.
+- FRESHNESS: The preference fake now materializes a distinct manager after every successful save. Stale retries re-evaluate unrelated, unmarked, and `Int.max` future replacements without mutating them, and verification rejects a distinct persisted manager whose canonical fields do not match the requested write.
+- VERIFICATION: The focused repository suite passes 23 tests. `make validate-core` passes boundary/native-package checks, 241 tests in 24 suites, and the post-test build; strict Swift format lint, `git diff --check`, and board validation pass. Generic iOS Simulator and macOS adapter builds both succeed.
+
+### 0351 — Owned VPN preferences are shared policy with thin platform clients (TASK-260715-15vkvz)
+- DECISION: `ReluxTunnelCore` owns the serialized exact-predicate repository, immutable canonical configuration, 15-second callback tokens, stable errors, one-stale retry, and reload verification. The iOS/macOS adapter modules only translate public `NetworkExtension` objects and notifications into the injectable core seams.
+- SAFETY: Ensure never enables; the explicit enable result names the OS-level possibility that another enterprise VPN is disabled. Duplicate repair removes every freshly revalidated current-schema inactive exact-owned manager, reloads after each removal, proves zero, then recreates one. Unmarked, unrelated, wrong-type, corrupt duplicate, active duplicate, and future-owned managers are zero-write paths.
+- IDENTITY: The complete host/provider/App Group/Keychain `PlatformVPNIdentity` remains injectable for deterministic fixtures. Both production factories fail closed until `TASK-260715-ypo7yo` supplies accepted signed bindings; no guessed identifier landed.
+- VERIFICATION: 18 deterministic Swift Testing cases cover mixed managers, type confusion, least-data/secret exclusion, idempotency, explicit enable/disable/remove, duplicate repair, future preservation, stale replacement, authorization, save/reload failure, timeout/cancellation late callbacks, and stop timeout. `make validate-core` passes 236 tests in 24 suites plus build; strict format lint and iOS Simulator/macOS Xcode builds pass.
+
 ### 0320 — Provider routing and cleanup share one bounded generation owner (TASK-260715-1bp6eu)
 - DECISION: Both platform roots expose identical callback seams and delegate to one core actor. V1 accepts only the four read-only commands, requires a request UUID at the provider boundary, keeps at most 256 active and 256 recently completed request IDs, and retires pending once-only reply gates on stop so a late source callback cannot reach another generation.
 - CLEANUP: Every generation receives a fixed 64-handle cleanup registry. Stop immediately rejects work and fans out cancellation, then joins one reverse runtime stop behind an injected ten-second budget. Expiry force-closes registered controllable handles and records only the raw Apple reason, one fixed counter/gauge, and the finite `cleanup_deadline_exceeded` token. Provider fatal failure emits one stable 1001–1009 NSError and the later system stop joins the same cleanup.
